---
import MathLayout from '../../../layouts/MathLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../../utils/path';

const lang = 'en';
const currentPath = '/en/university/category-theory';
const title = 'Category Theory';
---

<MathLayout {title} {lang} {currentPath}>
	<article>
		<h1>{title}</h1>
		<p class="intro">Category theory is the "meta-language" of mathematics, studying the relationships between morphisms to provide a unified abstract framework for different areas of mathematics.</p>

		<h2>Why Learn Category Theory?</h2>
		<blockquote>
			<p>"Category theory is the mathematics that mathematicians invented to talk about mathematics."</p>
		</blockquote>

		<h2>Core Concepts</h2>
		<div class="concepts-grid">
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Objects</h3>
				<p>The basic elements of a category - can be sets, groups, topological spaces, or any mathematical object.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Morphisms</h3>
				<p>Arrows between objects, representing structure-preserving mappings.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Composition</h3>
				<p>Composition of morphisms, $g \circ f$ means first apply $f$, then apply $g$.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Identity Morphism</h3>
				<p>The identity arrow of each object, leaving the object unchanged.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Important Theorem</h2>
		<div class="theorem-card card">
			<h3>Yoneda Lemma</h3>
			<p>One of the most fundamental results in category theory, stating that an object is completely determined by its morphisms to other objects.</p>
			<div class="formula">
				<code>Nat(Hom(A,-), F) ≅ F(A)</code>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Learning Path</h2>
		<div class="learning-path">
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">1</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Category Foundations</h3>
					<p>Objects, morphisms, composition, identity, commutative diagrams</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">2</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Functors & Natural Transformations</h3>
					<p>Functors (mappings between categories), natural transformations (mappings between functors)</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">3</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Limits & Colimits</h3>
					<p>Products, coproducts, terminal object, initial object, fiber products</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">4</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Yoneda Lemma</h3>
					<p>Representation theorem, presheaves, sheaves, adjoint functors</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">5</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Monads & Algebras</h3>
					<p>Monads (Endofunctors), algebras, free structures</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Connections to Other Fields</h2>
		<div class="connections">
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">←</span>
				<span>Set Theory - Category of sets, functions as morphisms</span>
			</div>
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">←</span>
				<span>Group Theory - Category of groups, homomorphisms as morphisms</span>
			</div>
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">←</span>
				<span>Topology - Category of topological spaces, continuous maps as morphisms</span>
			</div>
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">←</span>
				<span>Algebraic Geometry - Category of schemes</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="nav-footer">
			<a href={getPath('/en/university')} class="back-link">← Back to University Math</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</MathLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	blockquote {
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
	}

	.concepts-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concept-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.concept-card p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.theorem-card {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1);
		border-color: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.3);
	}

	.theorem-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.theorem-card p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
	}

	.formula {
		padding: 1rem;
		background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
		border-radius: 8px;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.formula code {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: #a5b4fc;
	}

	.learning-path {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.path-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.path-step:last-child {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.step-num {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #eab308, #f97316);
		border-radius: 50%;
		font-weight: bold;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}

	.step-content h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.step-content p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.connections {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.connection-item {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 0.75rem;
		background: rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.05);
		border-radius: 8px;
	}

	.conn-icon {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		color: #eab308;
	}

	.nav-footer {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.back-link {
		color: #eab308;
	}
</style>
